---
/**
 * Terms and conditions for using this website.
 *
 * Deliberately narrow: these are website terms, not construction contract
 * terms. The company's actual obligations to a customer live in the signed
 * contract and estimate for that job, and a web page must not appear to
 * modify them. Section "These terms are not your contract" says so outright,
 * because a site that quietly implies otherwise is the real risk here.
 *
 * Original wording, as the client asked. Should be read by the company's
 * attorney before launch.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { business, legalUpdated } from '../content/idf';
---

<Page
  title={`Terms & Conditions — ${business.name}`}
  description={`The terms that apply to using the ${business.name} website.`}
  heading="Terms & Conditions"
  standfirst={`The terms for using this website. Last updated ${legalUpdated}.`}
>
  <section class="hp-section hp-section--tight">
    <div class="legal">
      <h2>These terms are not your contract</h2>
      <p>
        This page covers your use of this website and nothing else. If you hire us, the
        agreement between us is the written contract and estimate you sign for that job.
        Those documents govern the work, the price, the schedule and any warranty.
        Nothing on this website changes them, adds to them, or takes anything away from
        them, and where this page and your signed contract appear to disagree, your
        contract is the one that counts.
      </p>

      <h2>Using this site</h2>
      <p>
        You are welcome to read this site, and to use its forms to contact us about
        actual work. Please do not use it to send anything unlawful, to try to break or
        overload it, to scrape it automatically, or to submit forms in someone else's
        name.
      </p>

      <h2>Estimates and enquiries</h2>
      <p>
        Sending an enquiry through this site does not create a contract and does not
        oblige either of us to anything. It starts a conversation.
      </p>
      <p>
        We aim to provide a written estimate within 24 hours of visiting the site. An
        estimate is valid for the scope described in it and is subject to what we find
        once work begins — concealed damage behind a wall is the usual example. Where
        that happens we tell you, in writing, before the extra work is done.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is a price. We do not publish prices, and no page here is
        an offer capable of being accepted.
      </p>

      <h2>Offers</h2>
      <p>
        Where this site advertises an offer, it applies to new customers, to work
        contracted with us, and only where we have confirmed it to you in writing as
        part of your estimate. Offers cannot be combined with each other, cannot be
        applied to work already contracted or completed, and can be withdrawn or changed
        at any time. Ask us for the terms of a current offer when you request your
        estimate and we will confirm them to you before you commit to anything.
      </p>

      <h2>What is on these pages</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep this site accurate, but descriptions of our services are
        general. What we will do on your property is what your estimate says we will do.
        Photographs of completed work show that project, not a promise about yours.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reviews shown on this site come from Google and are the words of the people who
        wrote them. Where we show a selection of reviews, we show our overall Google
        rating and total review count alongside it, so the selection cannot leave a
        misleading impression.
      </p>

      <h2>Licensing, and what we do not do</h2>
      <p>
        {business.name} holds Virginia Class A contractor licence {business.license}.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not negotiate or settle insurance claims. Acting for a policyholder in
        negotiating or settling a claim is public adjusting, which is licensed
        separately in Virginia and is not something we are licensed for. We document
        damage, write our own estimate for your file, answer your insurer's questions
        about our own scope, and carry out the repair work.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are a contractor, not a real estate brokerage. Where this site mentions
        selling a home, we are describing renovation work that prepares a property for
        sale. If you need an agent we can introduce you to a licensed one; the listing
        is handled by them, and the work is handled by us.
      </p>

      <h2>Other people's websites</h2>
      <p>
        Where we link out — to a lender, to Google, to a social account — we are not
        responsible for what is on the other end of the link or for how that company
        handles your information.
      </p>

      <h2>Our content</h2>
      <p>
        The text, photographs and design on this site belong to us or are used with
        permission. Please do not republish them as your own. You are of course welcome
        to link to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided as it is. We are not liable for loss arising from using
        it, or from being unable to use it, or from relying on general information here
        instead of the written estimate we would give you. Nothing in this paragraph
        limits any liability that cannot lawfully be limited, and nothing in it affects
        our obligations under a contract you have signed with us.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of the Commonwealth of Virginia.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this page go to
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>, or call
        <a href={business.phonePrimaryHref}>{business.phonePrimary}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
